  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "Analytical and constructive: the document assumes the validity of both quantum mechanics and Reformed theology and seeks to find structural parallels.",
    "Q1_identity": "An isomorphism record (ISO-012) mapping the sign operator in quantum mechanics to moral orientation in Reformed theology.",
    "Q2_domain": "Lives at the intersection of quantum mechanics, operator algebra, and Reformed soteriology.",
    "Q3_claim": "The mathematical structure of a Hermitian operator with eigenvalues \u00b11 that commutes with all self-generated unitary operations maps onto the Reformed doctrine of total depravity and sola gratia: self-effort cannot change moral status; only external grace can.",
    "Q4_support": "Supported by quantum mechanical constants of motion, scriptural evidence (Romans, Ephesians, Matthew), and connections to other ISOs (ISO-002, ISO-003, ISO-004).",
    "Q5_dependencies": "Depends on the Reformed theological anthropology (binary moral status), the existence of a commuting operator \u03c3, and the validity of the six theorems of closed-system incompleteness from ISO-002.",
    "Q6_consequences": "Forces the conclusion that Pelagianism is mathematically impossible; predicts behavioral improvement without sign change; constrains soteriology to monergism or synergism with external grace.",
    "Q7_kill": "Would be destroyed by a genuine case of self-salvation (sign flip without external grace), evidence that moral orientation is continuous rather than binary, or a demonstration that [\u03c3, U_self] \u2260 0 for the relevant operator."
  },
